        "rationale": "The requirement has three directive obligations on the bundled skills. They must direct agents to (1) write site queries that select every place the obligation applies and no others, (2) write violation queries for every kind of construct that could break it, and (3) give every query `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions.\n\nThe marked test `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_direct_exact_site_queries_violation_queries_and_snippets]` covers all three. It reads the `## Do` section of the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md`. It does this through `distributed_reference`, `skill_file` and `section`, which collapses line wraps. It then asserts with `assert_text` that the section contains:\n- \"check that the site queries select every place the obligation applies and no others\" (obligation 1);\n- \"Write a violation query, with `within` naming the site query, for every kind of construct that could break the obligation\" (obligation 2);\n- \"Give every query `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions\" (obligation 3);\n- \"This applies to violation queries too.\", which ties the snippet rule to violation queries as well as site queries.\n\nThe guidance is a text artifact, so asserting that the directive text is present in the right section checks the behavior. `section` returns only the `## Do` body. It would fail if the guidance moved to a Don't list or was removed. The assertions use the same wording the requirement does. A weakened or dropped directive would fail them.\n\nThe companion test `bundled_skills_give_distributed_guidance_as_do_and_dont_lists` is marked for a different requirement, `requirements.cli.distributed_guidance.lists`. It does not change this verdict. The reference also contains the matching Do paragraphs, which I read. No fixme acknowledgments apply, and I found no gap."
